post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
RDE services are started by the per-user supervision daemon.

To enable it for the current user:
  systemctl --user daemon-reload
  systemctl --user enable --now rde-daemon.service

The daemon detects the installed service binaries (rde-brightness,
rde-volume, rde-theme) and spawns them itself, so the per-service units
shipped in the repository are optional and should not be enabled alongside
it.

Brightness changes are written directly to sysfs by rde-brightness. Add your
user to the video group so the service can write /sys/class/backlight:
  sudo usermod -aG video $USER
For external monitors, also grant access to /dev/i2c-* (commonly the i2c
group), then log out and back in.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}

pre_remove() {
  cat <<'EOF'
If you enabled RDE in this account, stop the user daemon before removing the
package:
  systemctl --user disable --now rde-daemon.service
EOF
}
